    "text": "<p>Two identical blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> resting on the smooth horizontal floor are connected by a light spring of natural length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>. A third block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moving with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> along the line joining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> collides with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.The maximum compression in the spring is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0100_9cbf2eab9308.png\" style=\"width: 602px; height: 71px;\" /></p>"
